menu "Pocket character"

    config POCKET_WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi network name"
        default ""
        help
            Put real credentials in sdkconfig.secrets (ignored by git), not here.

    config POCKET_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Wi-Fi password"
        default ""

    config POCKET_SERVER_URL
        string "Server WebSocket URL"
        default "ws://192.168.1.171:8790/ws"
        help
            The computer running pocket-server, on the same Wi-Fi. ws:// only on a trusted LAN.

    config POCKET_TOKEN
        string "Server token"
        default ""
        help
            Must match POCKET_TOKEN on the server when it binds a LAN address.

    config POCKET_DEVICE_ID
        string "Device id sent in hello"
        default "pocket-a1"

    config POCKET_ENABLE_AMPLIFIER
        bool "Drive the amplifier (GPIO5 SD) during replies"
        default n
        help
            Off: the amplifier stays in shutdown and replies are silent (eyes still animate).
            On: the amplifier is enabled only while speaking, after silent clocks and the
            startup delay, exactly as the Step 11 build does. Enable it only on the wired,
            qualified speaker path.

    config POCKET_MAX_VOLUME
        int "Volume cap (0-65)"
        range 0 65
        default 65
        help
            Builder decision 2026-09-30: up to 45 may drive the speaker directly (2.20 V
            worst-case peak at the amplifier's highest gain, against the speaker's 2.53 V limit).
            Builder decision 2026-10-26: 65 is the permanent cap, on the basis that the GAIN pin
            is left open (9 dB), where full scale is 5.43 V peak and cap 65 gives 2.29 V peak;
            measured 2.06 V on normalised speech. The firmware refuses anything above 65, and
            the figure is wrong if GAIN is ever strapped higher.

    config POCKET_AMP_STARTUP_DELAY_MS
        int "Silent clocks before enabling the amplifier (ms)"
        range 1 10000
        default 100

    config POCKET_TX_POWER_QDBM
        int "Wi-Fi transmit power cap, quarter dBm (34 = 8.5 dBm)"
        range 8 80
        default 34
        help
            Board A1's chip antenna only worked once capped at 8.5 dBm (2026-09-21).
            Applied after every radio start.

    config POCKET_MIC_SHIFT
        int "Microphone 32-bit to 16-bit shift (gain)"
        range 8 16
        default 12
        help
            The INMP441 puts 24 bits in a 32-bit slot. Shifting by 16 is unity; 12 is 16x gain.

    config POCKET_DISPLAY_FLIP
        bool "Rotate the screen 180 degrees"
        default n
        help
            In the brass harness the OLED's header edge faces the front of the device, which
            is upside down for the panel's default scan. Turn this on if the eyes appear
            upside down; it mirrors both axes in the SSD1306 driver, nothing else changes.

endmenu
